🏦 BofA Mapping (Networking)

Relating this to your project:

Your CPS Payment Receiver microservice should communicate with other internal services using ClusterIP Services, not Pod IPs.

External bank traffic enters through enterprise infrastructure (reverse proxy/load balancer), then reaches OpenShift Routes or Services.

During pod restarts or scaling, networking continues to work because clients use the Service DNS name, not individual pod addresses.

This is why your application should never cache or depend on a specific pod's IP..
